#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Builds libmpv for Bloom from pinned sources into vendor/mpv/lib.

One library comes out: libmpv.2.dylib, with FFmpeg, libass, libplacebo,
dav1d, Lua, mbedTLS and the rest linked in statically, for arm64 and
macOS 14.0 or later. It links nothing outside /usr/lib and /System, so
the app bundle needs no Nix store and no Homebrew.

    dev/build-mpv            builds what is missing, then fills vendor/mpv/lib
    dev/build-mpv --clean    deletes the build folder first

Every source is a release tarball with its SHA-256 below, or a git tag
with its commit; a mismatch stops the build. The build folder
(BLOOM_MPV_BUILD_DIR, default vendor/mpv/build) keeps the tarballs, the
install prefix and a stamp per component, so a second run builds only
the components whose recipe changed. CI caches that folder keyed on this
file. The build tools (meson, ninja, cmake, pkgconf) come from a Python
venv in the build folder, so every machine builds with the same versions;
the rest is Xcode's clang, make and git.
"""
